.TH CBMAP_GET 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cbmap_get \- get value by key (type-inferred, returns value)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cbstmap.h>

value = cbmap_get(hm_name, key);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Type-inferred wrapper for cbmap_get_elem_ref(). It returns the value itself.
It calls ccol_fatal_err() if the key is not in the map. It also calls
ccol_fatal_err() if the two sizes do not match.

The lookup key goes through the DECLARED key type of the tree, in the
same way as in cbmap_insert(3). A key that the tree stored through that
conversion is only ever found again by a lookup that makes the same
one. A literal and a computed expression are both accepted.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
hm_name  BST map to search
key      Key to look up
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Returns the value of that key
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The macro returns the value, not a pointer
For a string, the macro returns the char* itself
The macro stops the program if the key is not in the map
The macro stops the program with ccol_invalid_args if key is a NULL
character pointer, which is not a string
The macro stops the program if the size of the stored value does not
match the size of the declared value type
The search takes O(log n) time
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cbmap_get_ptr (3),
.BR cbmap_insert (3)
